<title>USA: ARCO, Syntroleum in license pact.</title>
<headline>ARCO, Syntroleum in license pact.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Syntroleum Corp said Atlantic Richfield Co signed a non-exclusive master license agreement for its Syntroleum process used to convert natural gas into synthetic crude oil and transportation fuels.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, ARCO received rights to use the process in broad geographic areas, including Alaska, the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are very enthusiastic about the opportunities for applying this technology to ARCO's gas reserves around the world,&quot; ARCO senior vice president Skip Bilhartz said. &quot;It should help us drive ARCO's growth agenda.&quot;</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
